from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,re
ROOT=Path('/workspace/scratch/9c0c54a66f6c/agents/p15')
PKG='MPL_15_195-228+18_002-017'
source=json.loads((ROOT/'entries_source.json').read_text())
items=[]; verdicts=[]
def add(n,kind,loc,quote,statement,reconstruction,reason,check='agrees',verdict='kept',merge=None):
    # All text below is manually authored after reading the full entries and passages.
    ident=f'SA07-{merge or n}'
    verdicts.append(dict(entry_id=f'{PKG}#{n}',item_id=ident,verdict=('merged into '+ident if merge else verdict),reason=reason))
    if merge:
        next(i for i in items if i['id']==ident)['sources'].append(f'{PKG}#{n}')
        return
    cotes=list(dict.fromkeys(x.split('/')[0] for x in loc.split(';') if '/' in x))
    items.append(dict(id=ident,sources=[f'{PKG}#{n}'],kind=kind,cote=cotes,scans=loc,
        lines=PKG+'_transcription.tex: '+loc,his_words=quote,statement=statement,
        reconstruction=reconstruction,check=check,check_reason=reason))

add(1,'reading question','16/044–051:L1717–1882 (other package)','A; B; C; D','The manuscript letters must be identified by their definitions and implications: algebraic Lefschetz, inverse Lefschetz, numerical/homological comparison and projectors are distinct assertions.','The comparison with the 1969 published lettering is editorial; none of these definitions occurs in this package.','The table explicitly labels two matches provisional. The p16 reader checked the cited correspondence sheets; the present package only invokes Hodge and Tate at 15/215. No four-letter dictionary is claimed to be written here.')
add(2,'other','15/213:L433–438;15/215:L475–498;15/227:L877–879','conj. de Hodge et de Tate','This is an earlier-run comparison table of linear motivic reconstruction with nonlinear anabelian assertions; its four rows have distinct bases, objects and hypotheses.','The Tate/anabelian, centre, real-section and cusp comparisons belong to the earlier run, not these manuscript pages.','The pages ask about motivic realization and map recovery. They do not state the cited anabelian theorems. Retained as a contextual synthesis, with individual comparisons indexed separately.')
add(3,'other','15/213:L406–438;18/011:L1078–1153','G(X,ξ)=Aut(ξ); Isom(T_B⊗k,T_DR)','A modern comparison matrix separates Tannakian reconstruction, Nori/Ayoub group comparison, pure semisimplicity, arithmetic descent, algebraic cycles, Hodge fullness, periods and integral/crystalline questions.','Every modern theorem in the matrix is an earlier-run comparison, not an assertion by Grothendieck on these sheets.','The text defines automorphism groups and period torsors but supplies no Nori/Ayoub construction. The table correctly preserves the additional hypotheses; bibliographic claims are rechecked separately.')
add(4,'unproved claim','15/195:L13–19','Ils ne sont en général pas isomorphes, sans doute','For a characteristic-p geometric point y with perfect residue field k and a characteristic-zero point x, compare the crystalline fibre ξ_y,p with ξ_x,p⊗Zp W(k). The author tentatively expects nonisomorphism in general and a qualified finite-k exception.','Which tensor, integral and Frobenius structures an isomorphism must preserve is not specified. The uncertain finite-field qualification is not reconstructed.','Both the tentative wording and deleted verification mark are visible. Oda degree-one results cannot settle this unspecified mixed-characteristic comparison.')
add(5,'reading question','15/195:L21–23','ne provient pas d’une filtration du motif','The de Rham realization has a Hodge filtration distinct from an intrinsic motivic filtration, reportedly trivial on simple motives.','The associated-graded coefficient Q_l and the level/weight indexing remain uncertain; no modern filtration is silently substituted.','The margin explicitly distinguishes the two origins. Its doubtful Q_l is retained as a scan issue, not used to equate Hodge and motivic filtrations.')
add(6,'unpursued implication','15/197:L51;15/201:L126–140','Il n’y a plus en général d’opération de π₁(X)','Field automorphisms give semilinear descent on de Rham fibres; this alone does not furnish an action of the manuscript π₁(X) on an integral or de Rham fibre.','A monodromy action requires a specified local system and base point, additional to field descent.','Both passages explicitly distinguish semilinear coefficient-field action from fundamental-group action. The note preserves that distinction.')
add(7,'reading question','15/197:L53','H^{2|1}(Q_l,G_l)','After choosing one fibre functor, its locally isomorphic forms are represented by H¹ of its tensor automorphism group. Neutralization of the entire gerbe is a different obstruction problem.','H¹ is a mathematical alternative suggested by the context, not a recovered reading of the uncertain exponent.','The transcription actually preserves 2|1. The note correctly refuses to decide the ink from the torsor interpretation.')
add(8,'unproved claim','15/197:L53–55;15/199:L77','pas d’isom canonique prévisible','There is no asserted canonical Q_l-comparison between the rational de Rham fibre and the l-adic fibre; even existence is questioned, especially with their descent/integral structures.','Nonisomorphism cannot be inferred from absence of an integral lattice alone; the coefficient category must be specified.','The manuscript separates noncanonicity from possible nonexistence and mentions weight/level zero. The note does not replace this with a comparison over a larger period ring.')
add(9,'unpursued implication','15/199:L79–100;15/201:L126–140','isom canonique « involutif »','A complex realization has an integral Betti lattice, whose Z_l and C extensions give the l-adic and analytic de Rham fibres; conjugation identifies the corresponding conjugate fibres involutively.','For smooth proper geometric realizations, these are the usual comparison maps. No assertion that the lattice determines the place follows.','The stated comparisons and involution are present. The later false-place-separation claim is a separate item.')
add(10,'self-flagged step','15/203:L162–177','τ=τ′τ″=τ″τ′; à vérifier','For a variety over R, under Betti–de Rham comparison, Betti scalar conjugation c_B and de Rham descent conjugation c_DR commute, and their linear product is the action of complex conjugation on Betti cohomology.','The modern formulation assumes a real model and the natural comparison. Two arbitrary semilinear involutions need not commute.','The verification mark attaches to the commuting-product identity. It is an unfinished compatibility check on the page, not a purely formal semilinearity fact.')
add(11,'self-flagged step','15/203:L179–184;15/205:L210','frobenius en la place réelle; à vérifier','The real-conjugation action on the Betti lattice should match the order-two real decomposition-group action on its l-adic extension.','This uses functorial Betti–étale comparison for a real geometric object and compatible embeddings. It is not finite-field Frobenius.','The second verification mark is separate from the first; the continuation asserts the action without supplying its proof.')
add(12,'conjecture','15/205:L212–221','le dernier sous-espace … est motivique','A rational intersection of a Hodge-filtration term and its real-Frobenius translate is proposed to equal a motivic level subobject.','The strongest precise modern comparator is a generalized Hodge/coniveau assertion after defining the level index and replacing a mere rational intersection by an appropriate Hodge substructure. No exact equivalence is asserted.','The formula and submotive conclusion are written, but the index is uncertain. The note correctly declines to identify a fully specified generalized Hodge conjecture.')
add(13,'idea of the earlier run','15/205:L216–221','provient d’un sous-motif','A necessary condition for a rational subspace to come from a submotive is that its complexification be a sub-Hodge structure. A rational intersection lying in a Hodge band need not satisfy this.','The necessary-condition test is an earlier-run idea; it is not a counterexample to an unambiguously defined manuscript level convention.','The passage asserts motivicity of the intersection. The note accurately proposes a test without alleging that the author made a proved false geometric claim.')
add(14,'withdrawn in the same text','15/207:L253–255;15/219:L642–674;15/221:L720–734;15/225:L836','Je pense … non isomorphes; faux, cf groupoïde fondamental sur Z','The unrestricted expectation that distinct archimedean places have nonisomorphic bare integral or real fibre functors is explicitly retracted. Subsequent path/spreading arguments give isomorphisms in stated cases.','The retraction does not settle the narrower number-field separation or Hodge-enriched variants.','The circled false annotation is explicit at 207; 225 explicitly says a place is far from characterized by the Z-module functor.')
add(15,'conjecture','15/207:L259–261','T_α(R)=∅ pour α grand','In positive characteristic the author expects no real-valued fibre functor on sufficiently large finite motivic pieces and asks about totally real extensions.','A precise sufficient obstruction is a supersingular elliptic h¹ of categorical dimension two with quaternionic endomorphisms ramified at infinity; this is a reconstruction, requiring that object and all endomorphisms in the category.','The page gives neither a finite subcategory nor an obstruction. The note correctly marks this as a conjecture; the quaternionic argument and cote15/052 are separate modern checks.')
add(16,'reading question','15/207:L267;15/209:L283','catégorie fibrée … fpqc; c’est un torseur','Fibre functors form a gerbe, whereas tensor-isomorphisms between two fixed fibre functors form a torsor when locally nonempty.','The gerbe/torsor separation is modern terminology clarifying the passage, not a change to the transcribed word.','The text moves directly from category fibred over fpqc schemes to torsor. The note identifies the two different objects correctly.')
add(17,'unproved claim','15/209:L283','tous les autres pts s’en déduisent par des fibrés principaux','Relative to a chosen fibre functor ω, other fibre functors are obtained by twisting ω by torsors under Aut^⊗(ω).','This is precise for neutral Tannakian categories over a field, including their R-valued fibre functors; a category intrinsically over Z requires its own reconstruction hypotheses.','The manuscript states the twisting construction but supplies no descent proof or integral exactness assumptions.')
add(18,'conjecture','15/209:L285–300;15/211:L350–355','Il semble … biunivoquement; structure supplémentaire','Enriched transcendental motivic points over Z, R or C are proposed to correspond to complex points of X modulo conjugation.','The enrichment and geometric essential image are not specified. The proposal must not be identified with the already retracted bare-lattice separation.','The bracketed extra-structure phrase is essential and present; the later Questions sheet keeps the proposal open.')
add(19,'self-flagged step','15/211:L336–369','Questions; À revoir; F,V','The author proposes characteristic-p geometric points as Witt-valued motivic points with Frobenius/Verschiebung, and generalized filtered points in the residue field.','Perfectness, integral versus isogeny coefficients, and a geometric essential-image criterion are additional hypotheses. Oda covers abelian degree one only.','The heading and review mark govern these arrows. They are a programme, not a proved classification.')
