add(21,'reading question','15/213:L404–431','Groupe fondamental motivique discret; Comparaison avec π₁','The discrete motivic group is defined as Aut^⊗(ξ)=G_ξ(Z), with a proposed comparison to a topological fundamental group.','Equality with π₁^top is neither a definition nor a consequence of Tannakian reconstruction; a monodromy map would be additional data.','The definition and a separate comparison question are visible. The note correctly distinguishes these from Künneth-projector π_i in cote16.')
add(22,'unproved claim','15/213:L411–415','En vertu de Borel-Harish … nb fini','For fixed finite tensor piece α, finitely many isomorphism classes of integral fibre functors are asserted, followed by a question whether their discrete automorphism groups are isomorphic.','One must specify a finite-type integral group, allowed torsors/forms and the exact arithmetic class-number or orbit problem.','The handwritten appeal to Borel-Harish gives no such identification. The note appropriately withholds a general finiteness theorem.')
add(23,'unproved claim','15/213:L433–438;15/215:L475–481','Résulte de la conjonction des conj. de Hodge et de Tate … X normal','For normal connected X over C, or an algebraically closed subfield, the author asserts conditional full faithfulness of motives realized as discrete-motivic-group modules with Hodge structure.','A modern exact formulation requires the category of relative motives, monodromy and specialization hypotheses; finite-field Tate and Hodge fullness are separate inputs.','The dependency on both conjectures and normality is explicit. The note does not replace the assertion with the narrower abelian Hom theorem.')
