add(47,'unpursued implication','18/005:L966–974','cristal filtré','A filtered-crystal description of p-divisible groups or local geometric objects needs an essential-image condition.','Weakly admissible filtered (φ,N)-modules classify semistable p-adic representations under Colmez–Fontaine hypotheses; N=0 gives the crystalline case. A p-divisible group further restricts the weights and integral structures.','The note matches a precise later comparison while refusing to equate arbitrary filtered crystals with geometric motives.')
add(48,'unpursued implication','18/005:L966–974;18/011:L1081–1084','groupes p-divisibles mod isogénie','Oda’s comparison identifies the Dieudonné module of the p-torsion of an abelian variety over a perfect field of characteristic p with its first de Rham cohomology, including its Hodge sequence.','This is a later theorem used to delimit the local programme; it does not identify all motives, lifts or local-field representations.','The note’s scope is exact: first cohomology of abelian varieties in characteristic p, distinct from the local-field essential-image question.')
