add(53,'reading question','18/009:L1047–1065','W_i(E(n))=W_{i+2n}(E); F^i(E(n))=F^{i+n}(E)','The stated Tate convention gives Gr_i^W(E(−1))=(Gr_{i−2}^W E)(−1); the later unshifted associated-graded formula is incompatible with it.','The correction is a mathematical alternative only. The separate ± ambiguity in the preceding E(−1) line also needs the scan.','The index problem follows directly from the written shift and is not cured by the abstract lattice remaining unchanged.')
add(54,'unproved claim','18/011:L1095–1116','Big → Fil; torseur','For a fixed tensor-filtration type on a reductive group in characteristic zero, filtrations and their splittings are modeled by G/B and G/L, with a relative unipotent torsor G/L→G/B. Their dimensions are g−b and g−ℓ.','B is a parabolic, U its unipotent radical and L a Levi, so b=u+ℓ. Identifying the manuscript’s functor of tensor filtrations with these spaces is an additional reconstruction.','The quotient dimensions agree under these hypotheses. The note appropriately separates a single vector-space splitting from the tensor-compatible homogeneous-space statement.')
add(55,'reading question','18/011:L1082–1084;18/011:L1099–1107;18/011:L1120–1121','Q = fibré des sous groupes de Lévi','Q is both an H′-reduction of an isomorphism torsor and the space of Levi subgroups, while H′ is the inverse image of a Tate G_m in B′/U′.','The first description has dimension u+1, the second u; a quotient or Tate normalization is needed to reconcile the bounds.','The note identifies an actual dimension discrepancy among the written definitions. No missing normalization is silently supplied.')
