add(57,'reading question','18/011:L1104;18/011:L1110','F → Φ induit A ≃ B','The main arrow forgets a splitting, Big→Fil, whereas a margin has the reverse arrow F→Φ.','The margin may concern only the finite étale type spaces; an actual reverse map would require a choice of splitting.','The directions differ on the page. The note correctly preserves the possible distinction between spaces and their types.')
add(58,'unpursued implication','18/011:L1101–1107','hom central (Tate); ε∘j=id','The displayed section j is central in the Levi quotient B′/U′ and splits its Tate character.','Neither a central lift in G′ nor the weight cocharacter of the whole category follows. A pure weight cocharacter has exponent ±2 on the ordinary Tate character, unlike the written identity.','The codomain of the centrality assertion is explicit. The note correctly separates the operator grading, Hodge splitting and tensor weight grading.')
add(59,'conjecture','18/011:L1125–1153','Conj. de transcendance forte; g+u','For k⊆Q̄, with K=k(α,β), ask whether trdeg_k K=dim G+dim U′.','This includes ordinary period genericity and additional independence of a Hodge-splitting comparison. It depends on resolving the Q/H′ normalization in SA07-55.','The strong equality is stated as a question and its field diagram is present. The note does not weaken it to ordinary Grothendieck period genericity.')
add(60,'idea of the earlier run','18/011:L1114–1127;18/011:L1137–1153','deg tr. … g; u; g−b; g−ℓ','Given the stated geometric upper bounds, maximal total transcendence degree forces equality in the component and quotient bounds by additivity in field towers.','This is an independent conditional derivation; it provides no evidence for maximality and is not applicable until the torsor dimensions are fixed.','The note’s calculation is correct conditionally and explicitly preserves the unresolved Q dimension.')
