add(62,'withdrawn in the same text','18/012:L1157–1179;18/011:L1135–1153;18/013:L1184–1188','la seule relation; dim G−1','The normalized period conjecture and elliptic determinant-one example on scan 012 are entirely cancelled; live related questions occur on 011 and 013.','Cancellation establishes neither a chronology between the sheets nor rejection of the mathematical truth. The normalization and field hypothesis remain uncertain.','The whole body is enclosed in deletion. The note correctly preserves it as a distinct cancelled witness.')
add(63,'unpursued implication','18/012:L1165–1170','sous-groupe engendré … dense','The cancelled draft infers a full algebraic generated group from genericity of a normalized comparison point.','The inference is valid if the comparison is Zariski generic in the specified normalized torsor and the generating subgroup is understood algebraically; it is conditional on that premise.','The margin is not an independent transcendence proof. The note correctly distinguishes its implication from the weaker live question.')
add(64,'reading question','18/012:L1172–1179','th. de Schneider','The cancelled non-CM elliptic example predicts transcendence degree three after determinant normalization.','Schneider’s classical period transcendence alone does not establish algebraic independence of three normalized quantities; Grothendieck’s published note 10 distinguishes these strengths.','The note correctly resists upgrading a marginal attribution into a proof of the entire proposed degree.')
