add(103,'unproved claim','18/016:L1241–1255','application formelle; diagonales','A linear map of the distribution modules is claimed to come from a pointed formal map exactly when it preserves the coalgebra diagonal and maps the degree-zero submodule onto the degree-zero submodule.','For finite free formal disks this is dual to a continuous augmented algebra map. The onto condition already makes a₀₀ a unit; diagonal compatibility makes it idempotent, hence1. Merely nonzero would not suffice over a general ring. The resulting map preserves the order filtration, not generally each homogeneous degree.','The note correctly requests the missing coefficient and chart conventions. Its alarm is resolved in the finite-free model by retaining the actual equality of degree-zero submodules, rather than weakening it to the printed nonzero consequence.')
